(Bug #77: `multiply` and `times` are two spellings of one operator, but
 two tokens, because `Repeat N times` claims the second. The append
 slot's operator list carried only the first, so `append v1 times v2 to
 l1.` reported "Expected 'to' after value in append statement" with the
 `to` written right there. All fifteen documented spellings now read the
 same in the append slot as everywhere else.)

a number called v1 is 12.
a number called v2 is 4.
a list called xs is [].

append v1 times v2 to xs.
append v1 multiply v2 to xs.
append v1 add v2 to xs.
append v1 plus v2 to xs.
append v1 subtract v2 to xs.
append v1 minus v2 to xs.
append v1 divide v2 to xs.
append v1 modulo v2 to xs.
append v1 mod v2 to xs.
append v1 remainder v2 to xs.
append v1 bit-and v2 to xs.
append v1 bit-or v2 to xs.
append v1 bit-xor v2 to xs.
append v1 bit-shift-left v2 to xs.
append v1 bit-shift-right v2 to xs.

(`times` binds like `multiply`: multiplication before addition.)
append v1 add v2 times 2 to xs.

Repeat 3 times, append -1 to xs.

Print "{xs's length} values".
Print element 1 of xs.
Print element 2 of xs.
Print element 16 of xs.
Print element 19 of xs.
Exit 0.
